Unless you have chosen a cryptographically secure password, it is recommended
to wipe it from the LUKS header now as hardware-based solutions provide
stronger security.

If you wish to delete other enrolled secrets later, you can do so by running:
systemd-cryptenroll --wipe-slot=<slot>

If you want to make sure that you have everything set up correctly, you can use
the above command for removing the password slot yourself after booting into the
system using the newly enrolled token(s) for the first time.
